<title>UKRAINE: Ukraine GDP drops 7.7 pct year-on-year in Jan-Apr.</title>
<headline>Ukraine GDP drops 7.7 pct year-on-year in Jan-Apr.</headline>
<dateline>KIEV 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ukrainian gross domestic product in the first four months of this year was 26.221 billion hryvnias, 7.7 percent lower than a year earlier, the Statistics Ministry said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>    UKRAINE GDP		 Jan-Apr 97   Jan-Mar 97   Jan-Apr 96</p>
<p> yr-on-yr pct change	  -7.7	   -7.9	   -9.6</p>
<p>Prime Minister Pavlo Lazarenko has forecast GDP will grow this year by 0.5-1.0 percent, which would be the first growth since independence in 1991. GDP fell 10.0 percent in 1996.</p>
<p>--Kiev Newsroom, +380 44 244-9150</p>
</text>
